  "body": "PR2540 gives a complete QQ16 native decoder but leaves precision open. This supplies a **sufficient local caller format for every prefix of its unchanged 2,463-event word**, at every positive payload tensor depth `lambda`.\n\nIf the real and imaginary components of each entry array lie in `2^-f Z` and have magnitude at most `H`, all declared caller boundaries lie in `2^-(f+4lambda+3) Z` and have magnitude at most\n\n```text\nH * (48 + 48*2^ceil(lambda/2) + 144*2^(4lambda))\n  < H * 2^(4lambda+8).\n```\n\nThus `4lambda+3` extra fractional bits and `4lambda+8` magnitude guard bits suffice. At one tensor layer the triangle envelope is `2448H`, with seven fractional and twelve magnitude guard bits. The proof uses quadratic-phase polarization ranks and exact finite inequalities over all 2,697 changed-field boundaries, 82,831 terms and 3,321 relative operators. Scalar coefficients stay unchanged under tensoring. A real-component box norm is used explicitly; Euclidean unitarity is insufficient for this claim.\n\nThe contract assumes exact atomic native children and cover maps, plus bounded physical entry arrays at the sixteen early and 224 current source entry times. Their independent temporal relaxation contains actual F0/B1 trajectories. It does not prove those entry bounds, child-internal precision, approximate-child stability, physical hosting or all-size supplier admission. Exact caller rounding at the stated boundaries is a no-op, preserving the retained exact endpoint/restoration result. The native word and invoice are unchanged. No new kappa is claimed.\n\nThe magnitude envelope is a conservative triangle bound, not a claimed attainable maximum. A saved `1/128` operator-term witness only rejects a six-bit **term certificate**; other same-source owner maps may cancel it, so no minimum precision for the full field is asserted.\n\nValidation on Windows, standard-library CPython 3.12.7:\n\n```sh\npython3.12 scripts/research_package.py --package research/qq16-caller-grid-reserve\n```\n\nThe registered suite passed: authenticated complete predecessor replay and its twelve controls; all-layer prefix certificates; independent direct Fourier sums for 548 quadratic forms and the complete C8 kernel; Git-free full export; three source corruptions rejected before retained import; and a typed bool/int receipt mutation. Separate AI proof/source/code review and optimized replay passed. No independent human review, proof assistant or hosted CI result is claimed.\n\nCanonical main was refreshed unchanged at `0fdd7d82de03e43c9e5a1000dfbcd380d1b687d2`, priority revision 4. The sole round selection seed `07b623645c5ad6daf10ad20d694abb79` selected recursive interfaces; `TASK.json` records the change from constructing another QQ16 interface to this named precision obligation. The required baseline and ceiling positive controls passed. PR2540 is pinned byte-exactly at `630d557af5088f66b45c447969cee9576600e50b`; its current head was reconfirmed before commit.\n\nOverlap evidence comprises the complete cached 768 open PRs at 15:00 UTC and 1,232 Discussion records at 15:03 UTC, supplemented with 50 current updated open PRs and six exact predecessor/precision bodies at 15:48 UTC. PR2546 is an odd-factor unread-minor admission audit; PR2096/2166 address Hilbert-defect accumulation in different P104 words. This package does not transplant their constants. The original parallel batch ledger was inspected read-only. This coverage does not reveal every unpublished investigation.\n\nCredit Ali Romman and the retained QQ16 lineage; ywz65's PR2511/2512/2540 native decoder work; thakrarsagar/PR2470 and starship-s/PR2443 for L2 and F0/cut reconstruction. Original source bytes and notices remain. The elementary Fourier/Gaussian identities are standard; the new result is their source-bound all-prefix application. Prepared by **ywz65**, with substantial OpenAI Codex assistance in derivation, implementation, testing, writing and review. Apache-2.0.\n",
